ReadMe

Class Name: Main

Difficulty: Level 4 — Object-Oriented Scheduling System

Estimated Time: 150–210 minutes

Actual Time Taken: 187 minutes

Written by: Chanwoo Park

Problem
Build a university course registration system.

Program Flow
Create students and courses, register them, save the result,
reload it, and print the final report.

Class Responsibilities
- Main: Starts the program.
- RegistrationManager: Business logic.
- Student: Student information.
- Course: Abstract course.
- Registration: Registration record.
- FileManager: File persistence.

Requirements
- Prevent duplicate registrations.
- Enforce maximum course limit.
- Save and restore registrations.

Learning Objective
Practice object-oriented design, collections, inheritance, polymorphism, exception handling, and file I/O.